        {
          "id": "20133064-cbac-4bb1-b3f9-78731d45204e",
          "name": "Lists all jobs that match the specified filter",
          "request": {
            "name": "Lists all jobs that match the specified filter",
            "description": {
              "content": "Lists all jobs matching the filter criteria specified in the JSON body.\n\n### Job fields available for filtering and sorting\\:\n\n| Field name        | Type    | Description / Possible Values            |\n| ----------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| BeginTime         | String  | Job start date and time                  |\n| BytesCollected    | String  | Bytes collected so far                   |\n| BytesToCollect    | Long    | Total bytes to be collected              |\n| CaseName          | String  | Case name                                |\n| CollectionID      | Long    | Collection ID number                     |\n| CollectionName    | String  | Collection name                          |\n| ComputerID        | String  | Computer ID number                       |\n| ComputerName      | String  | Computer name                            |\n| CustodianID       | Long    | Custodian ID number                      |\n| CustodianName     | String  | Custodian name                           |\n| Destination       | String  | Destination path                         |\n| DestinationType   | String  | Destination type, one of                 |\n| EndTime           | String  | Job end date and time                    |\n| ID                | Long    | Job ID number                            |\n| Label             | String  | Label value associated with this Job     |\n| NumErrors         | Long    | Number of errors encountered so far      |\n| NumFilesCollected | Long    | Number of files collected so far         |\n| NumFilesToCollect | Long    | Total number fo files to collect         |\n| NumWarninings     | Long    | Number of warnings encountered so far    |\n| PausedMinutes:    | String  | Number of minutes to job has been paused |\n| Priority          | String  | Job priority number                      |\n| ProgramName       | String  | Name of program performing the job       |\n| ReportingTime     | String  | Date and time of last job status report  |\n| Stage             | String  | Job stage                                |\n| Status            | String  | Job status (see list below)              |\n| SubmitTime        | String  | Date and time job was sbmitted           |\n| TargetID          | Long    | Target ID number                         |\n| TargetName        | String  | Target name                              |\n| TaskName          | String  | Task name                                |\n| TaskNumber        | Integer | Task ID number                           |\n| TotalTasks        | Integer | Total number of tasks in this job        |\n\n\n### Job status values\\:\n\nAwaiting Resource, Cancelled, Cancelling, Failed, Finished, Paused, Pausing, PickedUp, Ready, Resumed, Resuming, Running, Suspended, Suspending, Waiting",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "v2",
                "jobs"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "offset",
                  "value": "<integer>",
                  "description": "zero-based offset in the list of computers at which retrieval should start"
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "version",
                  "value": "<integer>",
                  "description": "version of the Jobs table, obtained from the last call to this function.\n\nThe Jobs table in the ECC Server database gets a new version whenever it is modified.\nThis version is returned in the response body for this query in the field `tableVersion`.\n\nIf `version` is supplied, it is compared to the current version of the Jobs table.\nIf the version numbers match, there is no updated data since the last call,\nand the query is aborted with a **204, 'No Content.'** response code."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "countOnly",
                  "value": "<boolean>",
                  "description": "if `true`, the total count for this query (ignoring `limit` and `offset`) is returned in the Response Body, with no other data.\n\nThis should be used ahead of the actual query to determine the total number of records in the response."
                }
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "description": "protocol for communication (This can only be one of http,https)",
                  "type": "any",
                  "value": "{{protocol}}",
                  "key": "protocol"
                },
                {
                  "description": "The location which the ECC resides",
                  "type": "any",
                  "value": "{{address}}",
                  "key": "address"
                },
                {
                  "description": "80, 443 or alternative",
                  "type": "any",
                  "value": "{{port}}",
                  "key": "port"
                }
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": null,
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"limit\": \"<integer>\",\n  \"jobId\": \"<integer>\",\n  \"sortBy\": \"<string>\",\n  \"ascending\": \"<boolean>\",\n  \"filters\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"<string>\",\n      \"value\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"<string>\",\n      \"value\": {}\n    }\n  ],\n  \"where\": \"<string>\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
